  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Features\n\nSpan parameters and returns (part of #201). Methods that take Span\\<T> or ReadOnlySpan\\<T> (by value, in, ref readonly, ref or out), or return one by value, no longer report IMP009:\n\nThe imposter copies the elements a span argument arrives with into an array.\n\nNew matchers in Imposter.Abstractions:\n\nSpanArg\\<T> and ReadOnlySpanArg\\<T> (Is(elements), Is(elements, comparer), Is(predicate), Any());\n\nOutSpanArg\\<T> and OutReadOnlySpanArg\\<T> for out spans.\n\nDelegates passed to Returns and Callback receive the span itself, by reference for ref and out.\n\nFor a span result, Returns takes the array the span covers.\n\nPRs: #205, #208, #213, #214.\n\nSpans in properties, indexers and events, and custom ref structs, still report IMP009 (see Limitations).\n\nFixes\n\nOverloads that differ only in passing a parameter by reference (#210, closes #209). Overloads such as Count(int) and Count(in int) got setups with the same signature, and the imposter didn't compile:\n\nthe overload declared first keeps the name;\n\nthe others get a numbered setup (Count\\_1), on the imposter and in the setup views.\n\nAwaitable methods with ref, out or in parameters (#212, closes #211). ReturnsAsync, ThrowsAsync and the default result of such methods didn't compile (CS1988).\n\nDocs\n\nCode links that opened the wrong test or line, and snippets that no longer matched their tests, are fixed (#207, closes #206).",
